TA-sensors
==========

Scripted-input add-on that collects Linux hwmon telemetry (the lm-sensors
data model) from /sys/class/hwmon - designed for BMC-less hosts where
IPMI/ipmitool is unavailable (consumer desktops, VMs, SBCs).

No third-party dependencies: stdlib-only python3, no ipmitool, no lm-sensors.

Inputs (both enabled by default, 60s interval):

  sensors_events.py   index=main     sourcetype=sensors:status
                      Nested JSON: {"chips": {"<chip>": {"<key>":
                      {"sensor_name","reading","reading_value","units","status"}}}}

  sensors_metrics.py  index=metrics  sourcetype=sensors:metrics
                      Ingest-time metric events named sensors.<chip>_<key>
                      (via METRIC-SCHEMA-TRANSFORMS) for mstats analytics.

Families collected: temp (celsius), in (volts), power (watts), current (amps),
humidity (percent_rh), fan (rpm). Raw milli-scaled hwmon inputs are normalized
by /1000 (fan stays raw rpm). A sensor whose "_alarm" latch is set reports
status "alarm", otherwise "ok".

Dashboards (app nav or Views):

  Sensors Overview   per-host reporting, current readings, non-ok/alarm table
  Sensors Metrics    mstats time-series: CPU cores, temperatures, fans,
                     voltages, power draw, live sensors.* metric count

Search quick reference:

  index=main sourcetype="sensors:status"
  | mstats avg("sensors.*") where index=metrics by metric_name span=5m

Configure interval/index by overriding default/inputs.conf in
etc/apps/TA-sensors/local/inputs.conf.

